    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Self-hosted n8n only:** this version uses the community node `n8n-nodes-ashdocs` (n8n verification pending), so it runs on self-hosted n8n. The HTTP version of the same template uses only built-in nodes and also runs on n8n Cloud.\n\n\n## Send escalating overdue invoice reminders with ASHDOCS, Gmail and Slack\n\nAnyone who invoices with ASHDOCS and wants overdue reminders to come from their own Gmail, in their own words, getting firmer the longer an invoice stays unpaid.\n\n### How it works\n1. At 09:00 every day the workflow lists every ASHDOCS invoice with status `overdue`, across all pages.\n2. **Choose reminder step** works out how many days overdue each one is and picks a step: 1–3 days **friendly**, 4–9 **firm**, 10 or more **final** (the limits live in **Settings**).\n3. **Skip reminders already sent** compares each invoice and step with the **Reminder log** sheet, so a customer gets each step once.\n4. Gmail sends the matching email with the amount, due date and pay link, the reminder is logged, and Slack gets one summary of what went out. A failed email posts its own Slack alert.\n5. Optional: the disabled **Invoice overdue** trigger sends the first reminder the moment an invoice becomes overdue. Turn it on if you are on a paid ASHDOCS plan.\n\n### Requirements\n- An ASHDOCS account (https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=overdue-reminders). The daily run works on every ASHDOCS plan, including Free (100 credits a month). The optional instant branch (ASHDOCS Trigger / webhook on invoice.overdue) needs a paid plan (Starter and up), which includes webhooks.\n- A Gmail account\n- A Google Sheets account\n- A Slack account\n- Self-hosted n8n with the community node `n8n-nodes-ashdocs` installed\n\n[ASHDOCS](https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=overdue-reminders) · [Docs](https://www.ashdocs.com/docs)",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "19437e57-0449-4cfe-a0b6-d2b8f162429a",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1160,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup\n**Plan:** The daily run works on every ASHDOCS plan, including Free (100 credits a month). The optional instant branch (ASHDOCS Trigger / webhook on invoice.overdue) needs a paid plan (Starter and up), which includes webhooks.\n\n1. Create an ASHDOCS account at https://www.ashdocs.com/?utm_source=n8n&utm_medium=template&utm_campaign=overdue-reminders and create an API key on the **API Keys** page of the dashboard. A test key makes watermarked test invoices while you try the workflow.\n2. Install the ASHDOCS community node: **Settings → Community nodes → Install**, enter `n8n-nodes-ashdocs`. Then open any ASHDOCS node and create the **ASHDOCS API** credential with your key.\n3. Create a Google Sheet with a tab named **Reminder log** and these columns in row 1: **Log Key, Invoice Number, Step, Days Overdue, Sent To, Sent At**. Pick it in **Read reminder log** and **Log reminder**.\n4. Connect Gmail in **Email customer**, and Slack in **Post summary** and **Reminder failed** (pick a channel).\n5. Fill in **Settings**: your name for the email sign-off, and the day limits if you want different ones.\n6. ASHDOCS can also send its own automatic reminders. If you use this workflow instead, turn those off (Invoicing settings → reminders, or `reminders_enabled: false` per invoice) so customers are not reminded twice.\n7. Optional, paid plan: enable **Invoice overdue** to send the first reminder right away.",
        "height": 580,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "32c489de-ef0d-4e13-a104-465152016700",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -580,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Customize\n- Rewrite the three emails in **Friendly reminder**, **Firm reminder** and **Final notice**.\n- Change the day limits in **Settings**, or add a fourth step with another Switch output.\n- Change the schedule time in **Every day at 09:00** (it uses the workflow timezone).\n- CC yourself, or send from a shared inbox, in **Email customer → Options**.",
